safeguarding original ownership, lineage, and sovereign attribution.


1. DEFINITIONS

1.1 "Nisaba"
    "Nisaba" means the Nisaba graphics engine and all components distributed
    as part of the Nisaba Engine by the copyright owner, including its source
    code, libraries, modules, renderers, layout systems, text systems, platform
    backends, codecs, and other engine components.

1.2 "Application"
    "Application" means software created by a user or third party that uses
    Nisaba through its permitted interfaces, APIs, libraries, or other
    integration mechanisms (whether statically or dynamically linked).

    An Application includes its own source code, assets, resources, logic,
    business logic, plugins, extensions, and other material created
    independently by the Application developer.

1.3 "Modification"
    "Modification" means any alteration, addition, deletion, replacement, or
    other change made directly to the source code of Nisaba, or any derivative
    engine work based substantially on Nisaba.

    A Modification includes, but is not limited to:
    - changing existing Nisaba source files;
    - adding code directly to Nisaba source files;
    - removing code from Nisaba source files;
    - changing the implementation of internal Nisaba components;
    - creating a modified version of the Nisaba source code;
    - creating a fork of Nisaba.

    Using Nisaba through its public APIs without modifying the Nisaba engine
    source files does not constitute a Modification.


2. GRANT OF USE

Subject to the terms of this License, the copyright owner grants the user a
perpetual, worldwide, non-exclusive, royalty-free license to use Nisaba for the
purpose of developing, building, testing, running, and distributing
Applications.

Permitted use includes:
- personal projects;
- educational and academic projects;
- open-source Applications;
- closed-source and proprietary Applications;
- commercial Applications and products;
- internal corporate software;
- products, embedded devices, and services built using Nisaba;
- distribution of Applications that use Nisaba.

The user may integrate Nisaba into an Application through any permitted
integration method, including both static linking and dynamic linking, without
subjecting the Application itself to this License.


3. DISTRIBUTION OF NISABA WITH APPLICATIONS

The user may distribute the authorized Nisaba components required by an
Application together with that Application, including precompiled binaries or
source code necessary for the Application to operate.

1. Unmodified Distribution:
   The user may freely distribute unmodified Nisaba components with any
   Application under Section 2.

2. Modified Distribution:
   Any distribution of a modified version of Nisaba, whether bundled with an
   Application or as a standalone engine, must strictly comply with the
   Reciprocal Copyleft obligations set forth in Section 5.


4. APPLICATION INDEPENDENCE & SOURCE CODE PROTECTION

The source code of an Application remains under the absolute control and
ownership of its author or applicable copyright owner.

Use of Nisaba in an Application (whether via static linking, dynamic linking,
or compile-time embedding) does not:
- transfer ownership of Application source code to Hussein Jaafar;
- require disclosure or publication of the Application's proprietary source code;
- require an Application to become open source;
- require an Application to be licensed under this License;
- require the author of an Application to publish modifications made to their
  own Application code.

An Application developer retains the exclusive right to choose the licensing
and commercial terms under which their Application is distributed.


5. RIGHT TO MODIFY & RECIPROCAL COPYLEFT OBLIGATIONS

Subject to the terms of this License, the user is granted the right to modify
the Nisaba source code, create derived engine works, and maintain forks of
Nisaba, provided that any such Modification satisfies all of the following
reciprocal conditions:

1. Share-Alike / Same License:
   Any modified version, fork, or derivative work based on Nisaba must be
   distributed strictly under the terms of this exact Nisaba Engine License.
   No recipient or distributor may re-license, sub-license, or apply
   closed-source/proprietary terms to Nisaba source code.

2. Public Source Disclosure:
   Anyone who distributes, conveys, or makes publicly accessible a modified
   version or fork of Nisaba (whether in source code, shared library, static
   archive, or compiled binary form) must make the complete corresponding
   source code of all modifications publicly and freely available under this
   License.

3. Preservation of Copyright Notices:
   All modified files and releases must retain intact all original copyright
   notices, author attributions, and license declarations pointing to
   Hussein Jaafar.

4. Prominent Modification Notices:
   Any modified source file must contain prominent notices stating clearly
   that the file has been modified, identifying the nature of the modifications
   and the date of modification.

5. No Additional Restrictions:
   No user or distributor may impose any further restrictions, licensing fees,
   or patent covenants that limit the freedoms granted by this License to
   downstream recipients.


6. PROHIBITED ACTS

The user may not:

1. distribute any modified version or fork of Nisaba under a proprietary,
   closed-source, or copyleft-incompatible license;
2. withhold, conceal, or fail to provide the complete source code of any
