7. APPLICATION DEVELOPMENT, PLUGINS, AND EXTENSIONS

A user is free to develop Applications, plugins, tools, and extensions using
Nisaba without obtaining separate permission.

The user may create:
- proprietary Application code;
- open-source Application code;
- commercial plugins and extensions;
- custom renderers or backends operating as independent modules;
- tools, asset pipelines, and editors.

Plugins, extensions, and custom modules developed independently that interface
with Nisaba through public headers or APIs do not constitute a Modification of
Nisaba and remain the exclusive intellectual property of their respective
creators.


